OUTPUT PATH RECONCILIATION (no silent drift — covenant #9)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The generated prompt names the output dir `apps/apple/TeslaSync/Features/Automations/**`.
That path does NOT exist in this repo and is NOT a project.yml source group. The repo's real,
compiled canonical page home is `apps/apple/Sources/Features/<Domain>/` — proven by every DONE
sibling page (AutomationsListPage, AutomationActivityFeedPage, ApiPlaygroundPage, … all under
Sources/Features/<Domain>). `Sources` is a project.yml source path (createIntermediateGroups),
shared by the iOS + macOS app targets (ADR-002). The page therefore ships at
`apps/apple/Sources/Features/Automations/**` — the faithful equivalent of the prompt's
`Features/Automations`. Strings ship in the platform catalog
`apps/apple/Localization/Localizable.xcstrings` (an allowed file). This mapping is the only
deviation from the literal prompt path and is recorded here per covenant #9 (identical to the
DONE sibling AutomationActivityFeed's reconciliation).

REUSE / DRY (engineering principles — no duplication of the proven domain core):
The pure, Foundation-only projection layer for this surface already ships, module-public, in the
P4 feature-view (`apps/apple/TeslaSync/feature-views/ActionBuilder.{Adapter,Catalog,JSON}.swift`):
the discriminated `AutomationAction` union, `AutomationActionKind`, `SettingValue(Kind)`,
`NotificationChannelSummary`, `ChannelOption`/`CommandOption`, `ActionCatalog`, the
`createDefaultAction`/`defaultChannelId`/`channelOptions`/`commandOptions`/`actionWithSettingValue`/
`displaySettingValue`/`commandParamsSeed`/`jsParseIntOrZero` helpers, and the order-preserving
`ActionJSONParser`/`Formatter`/`Number` engine — all take an INJECTED `localize` closure. This unit
REUSES that core (one source of truth, zero type collisions — new symbols are all `ActionBuilderPage*`)
and feeds it a `Localizable.xcstrings` localizer, then ships a fresh page/model/views that resolve
every string from the platform catalog (the P7 string requirement). No feature-views file was edited
(out of allowed scope).

NAVIGATION (the unit is (unrouted)):
The web `ActionBuilder` is a composable SECTION the `/automations` builder page renders inline — NOT
a standalone route. So this unit does NOT take a top-level `AppRoute` (that would hijack a sibling
unit's route). Instead it ships a typed `NavigationDestination` seam —
`ActionBuilderPageLink` + `View.actionBuilderDestination()` + `ActionBuilderPageRouteRegistration.make(...)`
— that any `NavigationStack` adopts to deep-link the full-screen editor. No edits to the P4 shell
(AppShell/AppRoute/TeslaSyncApp) were made — correct for an unrouted unit (covenant #7).

